{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Discovered from\n\nCI run 32553346737 on Gerrit change 2065 (ticket d893-e003-0539-47fc): pytest (ubuntu-latest,\npy3.12) failed tests/unit/test_plan_review.py::test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes\nwith 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45-dirty)' != 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45)' — the -dirty\nsuffix flipped BETWEEN two build_manifest calls inside one test. The same test passes locally.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by deterministic reproduction)\n\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:497 stamps every manifest with\n`_signing.gate_code_version()`, which shells `git status --porcelain` on the rebar source\ncheckout PER CALL (src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:_gate_commit_sha). Two byte-equality tests\ncompare manifests built by SEPARATE calls:\n\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:965-966 (test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py:79 (equality of two build_manifest outputs)\n\nUnder pytest-xdist another worker that transiently creates/removes a file in the checkout\n(or any concurrent writer) flips the dirty-state between the calls, so the assertion compares\nracy live-git provenance rather than the file-scope/pins contract under test. Reproduced\ndeterministically: creating a scratch file in the checkout between the two calls makes the\nequality fail with exactly the CI diff.\n\n## Approach\n\nPin the provenance in the affected tests: monkeypatch\n`rebar.signing.gate_code_version` to a constant in both test functions — manifest.py binds\n`from rebar import signing as _signing` (manifest.py:475) and calls\n`_signing.gate_code_version()` at call time (manifest.py:497), so pinning the attribute on the\n`rebar.signing` facade module is what the call site actually resolves through; no production\ncode changes. The tests then assert the contract they exist for — file-scope back-compat and\npins default-equality — independent of concurrent working-tree state. No production behavior\nchange.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes pins gate_code_version and passes\n      even when a file is created in the checkout between its build_manifest calls — verified by\n      running the test with the reproduction interleaving.\n- [ ] The build_manifest byte-equality in tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py is pinned the\n      same way.\n- [ ] A repo grep shows no remaining test byte-compares two separately-built manifests without\n      pinning gate_code_version (the rebar.signing facade attribute)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787378859790911001,"uuid":"5d2e1393-38ab-4186-b95a-e1940b301975"}